title: Melissa Smith
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Sheep farmer at [[Willow Creek Farm]] Preserve in Pennsylvania, a Certified Organic farm.

She rotationally grazes a mixed flock of Shetland sheep among trees. That is [[Silvopasture]].

She also runs a wool mill on the farm, with machines for washing, picking, and carding. Sheep to skein, without the wool leaving the property.

So the farmer is also a manufacturer. Her wool could not compete with New Zealand imports if it had to be shipped around to be processed. Milled where it grows, it can.

The cushions of the [[Oka Chair]] use her undyed wool. The stuffing is [[Waste Wool]], the short and discolored fiber that can't be spun.

Worked with [[Common Objects]].
